      "created_at": "2018-05-16T15:01:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-05-16T15:01:00Z",
      "body": "Should IP addresses be anonymized at the output level or at the storage level? If it's done at the the output level, all visitors stats will continue to show accurate numbers. However, if it's done at the storage level, then unique visitors will probably not be completely accurate, e.g., \r\n\r\n    192.168.1.100 => 192.168.1.0  == 192.168.1.120 => 192.168.1.0",
